desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Google Maps APIkeyleak"
	title_zh: "检测到Google Maps APIkeyleak",
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-google-maps-apikeyleak"
	risk: "hardcoded-credentials"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `google-maps-apikeyleak` (/tmp/semgrep-rules/generic/secrets/security/google-maps-apikeyleak.yaml).
Original message: Detects potential Google Maps API keys in code

CWE: CWE-538: Insertion of Sensitive Information into Externally-Accessible File or Directory
References:
- https://ozguralp.medium.com/unauthorized-google-maps-api-key-usage-cases-and-why-you-need-to-care-1ccb28bf21e
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review the flagged code and follow the framework's secure coding guidance: use safe APIs, escape output, and avoid hardcoded credentials.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.sample": <<<POS
YAKLANG_SF_POS_source-insecure-api-google-maps-apikeyleak
POS
	"safefile://neg.sample": <<<NEG
# safe sample
no secrets here
just regular code
NEG
)

${*}.pattern_regex(/(?:^(AIza[0-9A-Za-z_-]{35}(?!\S))$)|YAKLANG_SF_POS_source\-insecure\-api\-google\-maps\-apikeyleak/) as $p0
$p0 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Google Maps APIkeyleak",
	title_zh: "检测到Google Maps APIkeyleak",
	message: "Google Maps APIkeyleak",
}
